  "extraction_notes": [
    "The supplied PDF SHA-256 is fbe2d17e4ed91161bcc8a52a51936a45844d1e68019838832162a1e564dc4340.",
    "The 25 \u00b0C transfer curve was digitized from p. 3 Figure 2 at VDS = 5 V. The separate 125 \u00b0C curve is present in the figure but omitted from the structured curve set because the extraction target is the 25 \u00b0C curve.",
    "The output curves were digitized from p. 3 Figure 1 for VGS = 3.5 V, 4.0 V, 4.5 V, 5.0 V, and 10.0 V. Datasheet Note E states pulses <300 \u00b5s and duty cycle 0.5% maximum.",
    "The Ciss, Coss, and Crss traces were digitized from p. 4 Figure 8. The electrical-characteristics table gives the associated bias as VGS = 0 V, VDS = 20 V, and f = 1 MHz.",
    "RDS(ON) publishes typical and maximum values at VGS = 10 V, ID = 20 A for TJ = 25 \u00b0C and 125 \u00b0C, plus VGS = 4.5 V, ID = 15 A at TJ = 25 \u00b0C. No minimum RDS(ON) values are published.",
    "The VSD table value is typical 0.7 V and maximum 1.0 V at IS = 1 A, VGS = 0 V. Figure 6 additionally shows typical body-diode curves at 25 \u00b0C and 125 \u00b0C; the structured body_diode value uses the typical table value.",
    "Published values not representable by the strict schema include IDSS maximum 1 \u00b5A at VDS = 40 V, VGS = 0 V, TJ = 25 \u00b0C and 5 \u00b5A at TJ = 55 \u00b0C; Rg typical 3.5 ohm and maximum 5 ohm at VGS = 0 V, VDS = 0 V, f = 1 MHz; Qg(10V) typical 27 nC and maximum 33 nC; Qg(4.5V) typical 14 nC and maximum 17 nC; Qgs typical 5 nC and maximum 6 nC; Qgd typical 6 nC and maximum 9 nC, with gate-charge conditions VGS = 10 V, VDS = 20 V, ID = 20 A; and trr typical 29 ns, maximum 38 ns plus Qrr typical 26 nC, maximum 34 nC at IF = 20 A, di/dt = 100 A/\u00b5s.",
    "Thermal resistance values not representable by the strict schema are R\u03b8JC typical 2.4 \u00b0C/W, maximum 3 \u00b0C/W, R\u03b8JA typical 18 \u00b0C/W and maximum 22 \u00b0C/W for t \u2264 10 s, and R\u03b8JA typical 44 \u00b0C/W and maximum 55 \u00b0C/W steady-state."
  ],
